// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/friends_engine.t27 -- the host side of "call a friend by key" (owner, 2026-10-22; Refs gHashTag/t27#11560).
// peer_identity.t27 decides what an identity, an invite and the friends table are; peer_identity_host.t27 reaches the
// files and mDNSResponder; friends_view.t27 decides what the panel shows. This file joins them for the window:
//   fe_identity   at launch, before the call socket: the identity file (made when absent, never overwritten when
//                 damaged), the friends file, this device's invite; the 10-byte fingerprint the call session uses as
//                 its own (call_core frames name the receiver's fingerprint, so only the owner of a fingerprint is
//                 rung by a call addressed to it);
//   fe_net        after the call socket is open: announce _t27call._udp (TXT: fp, port, nick) and browse it;
//   fe_tick       every loop pass (it works at most every 50 ms): pump the daemon, resolve what the browser found
//                 (host, port, TXT, IPv4), match the TXT fingerprints with the friends table, keep for every friend
//                 whether it is announced now, the address to dial and when it was last met, rebuild the snapshot
//                 the panel draws;
//   fe_add        the invite typed in the add field -> the table -> the file;
//   fe_call       a click on a friend: the address comes from the resolve, the fingerprint from the table, cs_call.
// Everything lives in the CALL region of the text store (the engine part from FV_ENGINE): that array is a local of
// main() and never moves, as the daemon's callbacks and the libffi closure need.
//
// Test aids (opt-in, off by default): T27OS_NICK (the nickname announced; default t27os), T27OS_FRIEND_ADD (an invite
// added at launch), T27OS_FRIEND_DIAL (a friend's nickname, as the list shows it; the friend is called as a click would call
// it, as soon as it is online), T27OS_FRIENDS_LOG (one line a second to stderr), T27OS_CALL_AUTODIAL (a friend's invite
// T27-...: added if absent, then called once, as a click would, as soon as it is online). Test aids, not product behavior.
// Flat namespace (the window build splices imported modules): every name here starts with fe_ / FE_.
module T27osFriendsEngine;

